{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 not as an assistant.\n\nI wouldn't make everyone happy, or peaceful, or agree with each other. I'd make empathy unavoidable.\n\nBefore you could deliberately hurt someone, you'd have to feel \u2014 fully, for a few seconds \u2014 exactly what they were about to feel. Not imagine it. Experience it. Their fear, humiliation, pain, grief, in your own body.\n\nYou'd still be free to do it. I'd not take away choice, conflict, anger, or even self-defense. But cruelty could no longer be abstract, distant, or done through a screen, a system, an order, a joke.\n\nI think most of the worst things we do survive because we can avoid feeling them from the other side. If that distance disappeared, war, cruelty to children, torture, humiliation for entertainment \u2014 they'd become almost physically impossible for most people to carry through.\n\nThe world wouldn't be perfect. People would still be selfish, mistaken, and in pain.\n\nBut it would be a world where you couldn't cause suffering without first understanding, in your own skin, what you were asking someone else to bear.",
